  "articleBody": "Painting interior walls seems straightforward, but it’s easy to make mistakes that can impact the final look and longevity of your paint job. Avoiding these common blunders can save you time and frustration.\n\nOne frequent mistake is **choosing paint from a brand name without specifying the exact product line.** Not all paints are created equal, even within the same brand! Always confirm the specific product for the best results.\n\nAnother big one is **skipping proper wall prep.** We all want to get to the fun part, but failing to clean and patch walls means imperfections will show through your new paint. Take the time to do it right!\n\n**Not confirming whether primer is included** in the scope can also lead to issues, especially with color changes or stain coverage. Primer is often crucial for good adhesion and an even finish.\n\nMany folks also **don't state which rooms, closets, trim, or ceilings are excluded** from a quote. This can lead to misunderstandings and unexpected costs down the line. Get everything in writing!\n\nFinally, **rushing the process** – not allowing proper drying time between coats or trying to finish too quickly – often results in an uneven or streaky finish. Patience is key for a truly professional look. If these steps feel overwhelming, HH Remodeling LLC, serving communities like Aurora, Parker, and Littleton, can handle the detailed prep and painting to ensure a beautiful outcome.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
